config PARTITION_GUARD
	bool "Partition Guard: protect NVRAM/persist/EFS from userspace writes"
	default y
	depends on SECURITY && BLOCK
	help
	  Data-driven LSM that denies write-opens and destructive ioctls
	  (discard/zeroout) on per-device partitions (NVRAM identity,
	  persist, EFS), matched by GPT label against a runtime list.

	  Scope discipline: ONLY partitions that are per-device unique
	  and never written by OTAs, fastboot, or recovery. Boot,
	  recovery, modem firmware and super are deliberately NOT
	  covered, so flashing and OTA flows can never be blocked.

	  List: compiled-in defaults, replaceable via
	  partition_guard.protect=, extensible via
	  partition_guard.extend=, switchable via
	  partition_guard.disable and sysfs.
